  "note": "Election of 12 members of Ballymoney Urban District Council on 15 January 1926; ten candidates came forward for twelve vacancies, and the two members with the highest votes at the previous election were declared re-elected. Printed 'No Contest'. Donaghey and M'Ilroy were declared re-elected as the two members with the highest votes at the previous election. M'Kee Dunlop and M'Elderry were new members. Addresses and occupations printed with the names are left out (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026). Returned unopposed."
